        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did paḻaṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: തുണി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തുണി (tuṇi) — \"cloth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തുണി is the plain, unceremonious word: the bolt on the shelf, the washing on the line, the rag in your hand. Tamil writes துணி (tuṇi) and means the same thing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Malayalam holds a dressier word for the same stuff — വസ്ത്രം (vastraṁ), out of Sanskrit — and it turns up on a wedding invitation rather than over a washing line. The native word does the daily work; the borrowed one does the ceremony."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That division of labour is worth watching for, because it repeats through this book: two words, one meaning, and the register telling them apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: a fruit and a cloth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "tuṇi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *tuṇi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
